# [[Introduction: Hook with the Okaterra chair story]] → [[SDCSC-a001: Introduction]]
#* <$transclude $tiddler='SDCSC-a001: Introduction' $type="text/vnd.tiddlywiki" $mode="block" />
#* This story is a reality — you can currently go out and buy chairs that are healthy for you AND for the planet. And what's cool is that there are plentiful options, all solving different aspects of todays problems in different ways exemplifying the same principles — those of the circular economy, of regenerative design, and of sustainability more broadly. We'll define sustainability usefully in a design context, we'll look at if sustainability is enough, and how we can start thinking not just about having "better" processes and materials, but actually repair the earth around us as we design new things. Move from extraction to regeneration. So we'll define design, we'll look at this regenerative concept, and then we'll follow the considerations of a single chair from idea to production with other chairs aiding us along the way.
